$$$John 3:16
<title type="x-s3">God's Love.</title> <div sID="p1" type="x-p"/> <hi type="super">16</hi> For God so loved the world, that he gave his <hi type="italic">only begotten</hi> Son. <div eID="p1" type="x-p"/> <div sID="p2" type="x-p"/> The gift of the Son shows <hi type="italic">divine love.</hi> <div eID="p2" type="x-p"/>
$$$John 3:0
<div sID="p1" type="x-p"/> This chapter opens the discourse with Nicodemus and sets out the doctrine of regeneration, a theme peculiar to the evangelist and treated here at length so that the reader may see the whole scope before the particulars are examined in their order.
 <div eID="p1" type="x-p"/>
$$$I Samuel 1:1
<div sID="p1" type="x-p"/> Elkanah and his family are described, that we may know the parentage of Samuel, whose history now begins and whose birth was an answer to prayer offered in bitterness of soul before the Lord at Shiloh.
 <div eID="p1" type="x-p"/>
